# vibekit/web/static/style.css bundle manifest
# Files concatenated in declared order at Docker build time.
#
# THE CASCADE MODEL (simplified 2026-08-31): SOURCE ORDER IS THE CASCADE.
# Exactly two @layers survive, `reset` and `tokens` (declared in 00-header),
# because those are the two sets that are MEANT to lose to everything. Every
# other file is unlayered, so a tie between two rules of equal specificity is
# decided by the order below — later file wins.
#
# It used to be five layers (reset, tokens, components, utilities, mobile),
# and the layer maze was a measured hazard: 50-mobile.css sat in @layer
# mobile where every rule LOST to the 21 unlayered feature slices, so the
# whole authored phone design (full-width toolbar, hamburger reveal) shipped
# dead. `scripts/css-cascade-audit.py --unlayer <file>` enumerates the flips
# for any layering change; unlayering mobile flipped exactly its own 16
# intended overrides, and unlayering components (10-shell-app) and utilities
# (30-utilities) afterwards flipped ZERO pairs — the layers were pure risk.
#
# Ordering rules that carry weight:
#   00-02  header (layer decl + @property defs), tokens, ui-primitives base +
#          skin (unlayered, skin wins by order), reset
#   03     base — shared element defaults; every feature file may override
#   10-29  feature stylesheets, split by feature. 10-shell-app is FIRST so
#          feature files override its shell chrome (chevrons, icon buttons)
#          by coming later at equal specificity.
#   30-40  utilities, a11y
#   50     mobile — the cross-surface shell rules for <=48rem, LATE so they
#          beat the feature slices. A surface-specific mobile override lives
#          in its feature file's own @media block instead (the house pattern;
#          see 15-input.css, 24-find.css, 28-docs.css).
#   60-61  MCP integrations; 61 also carries the hit-target floor, zero-
#          specificity on purpose so it only ever sets min-*
#   70     selection — the one selected-state treatment for every surface that
#          has one. LAST on purpose: each of its selectors carries real
#          specificity, so coming after every feature file is the only thing
#          that lets it beat their equal-specificity `:hover` rules. It
#          therefore owns the selected hover and press too.
00-header.css
